# A Lennard-Jones trajectory on domains against one domain, 200 steps of
# velocity Verlet (D[distributed-migration]); the program is in
# Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir. The state of the domains is a
# md_dist.state carried by scf.for; at every step md_dist.covered decides,
# for all domains at once, whether the halo is kept or the particles migrate
# and the halo is rebuilt.
#
# The output: the number of rebuilds and 1 if it is more than none and fewer
# than the steps (both branches ran); then, each as the absolute difference
# and 1 if it is within the bound times its scale, the positions (to the
# nearest image, against the edge 4.8), the velocities (against their
# largest component), the forces of the last step (against their largest
# component), and the potential, kinetic, and total energy (against the
# kinetic energy); the change of the total energy since the start on
# domains and on one domain (against the kinetic energy); and the fields
# carried through the branch of every step against those before it, in the
# order of the set: the velocities, forces, and masses (bound 0), and the
# positions (bound 1e-15 of the edge). The masses are not all equal, and the
# forces carried through a rebuild are not otherwise read, so these two
# catch a field given to the wrong particles. dist-trajectory-lj-drift.test
# runs 2000 steps.
#
# Bounds (docs/validation.md, Section 2). The scales are the edge, the
# largest velocity and force components, and the kinetic energy, none near
# zero here, so no absolute floor is needed (rule 2). The trajectory is
# compared with a baseline of rounding on the same system (rule 4): the same
# program on one domain of md_dist (grid 1 x 1 x 1) against the trajectory
# of md, which differ only in the order of their sums and in their force
# kernels, with no decomposition. Measured after 200 steps, relative to the
# scales, the largest over the routes on the CPU (RTX 4090 pending):
#
#                 baseline (1 x 1 x 1)    domains (all grids)    bound
#   double  x     5.7e-15                    6.1e-15                   2e-14
#           v     7.2e-14                    6.7e-14                   3e-13
#           f     5.1e-14                    5.9e-14                   2e-13
#           E     4.5e-15                    5.3e-15                   2e-14
#   mixed   x     5.4e-7                     5.4e-7                    2e-6
#           v     1.0e-5                     1.0e-5                    4e-5
#           f     4.9e-6                     4.9e-6                    2e-5
#           E     4.5e-7                     4.4e-7                    2e-6
#
# Each bound is three times the baseline, rounded up to one digit: domains
# may add their own order of summation, but nothing larger. In mixed the
# differences on domains are those of one domain. The carried fields are
# copies, the same arithmetic, so their bound is 0 (rule 5); the positions
# are wrapped, x - n L, a few roundings of the edge (half an ulp of 4.8 is
# 9.3e-17 of it; measured 1.9e-16). The change of the total energy in 200
# steps is 1.47e-4 of the kinetic energy on domains and on one domain, in
# double and in mixed, the fluctuation of velocity Verlet at the step 0.005;
# the bound 1e-3 is about seven times that of the existing route (one
# domain) and holds both.
#
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/2, 2, 2/; s/STEPS/200/; s/XTOL/2.0e-14/; s/VTOL/3.0e-13/; s/FTOL/2.0e-13/; s/ETOL/2.0e-14/; s/DTOL/1.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
#
# Through md_exec, in double and in mixed precision.
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/2, 2, 2/; s/STEPS/200/; s/XTOL/2.0e-14/; s/VTOL/3.0e-13/; s/FTOL/2.0e-13/; s/ETOL/2.0e-14/; s/DTOL/1.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-md-exec="functions=main" \
# RUN:     --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
# RUN: sed 's/GRID/2, 2, 2/; s/STEPS/200/; s/XTOL/2.0e-6/; s/VTOL/4.0e-5/; s/FTOL/2.0e-5/; s/ETOL/2.0e-6/; s/DTOL/1.0e-3/' %S/Inputs/dist-trajectory-lj.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --md-exec-assign-algebra --convert-md-dist-to-md-exec="functions=main" \
# RUN:     --convert-md-dist-to-loops %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_transforms \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-precision="mode=mixed" \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-algebra --md-exec-assign-storage --convert-md-exec-to-loops \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
